   },
   {
    "role": "fix3",
    "text": "So you add a bed of gravel on the return pipe, giving bacteria a place to live."
   },
   {
    "role": "name",
    "text": "This is a biofilter."
   },
   {
    "role": "how",
    "text": "Water flows through the gravel, bacteria eat the ammonia, and the pond turns clear."
   },
   {
    "role": "fact",
    "text": "Turning one gram of ammonia nitrogen into nitrate uses about 4.57 grams of oxygen from the water."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem3",
    "text": "But on a hot day, warm water holds less oxygen, so the fish crowd the surface, gasping."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix4",
    "text": "So you add an air pump that blows bubbles up through the water, and the oxygen climbs back."
   },
